Below is a quick summary of what’s happening and then two small “search / replace” patches for lib/features/modeling/behavior/ReplaceConnectionBehavior.js to make sure that whenever we call modeling.connect(…) in the replacement logic, we pass the correct parent (the container of the new target or new source). Without that hint the connection ends up in the wrong BPMN‐Diagram/participant.

1) Scenario & Root Cause  
   • When you replace a MessageFlow by a SequenceFlow between two different Participants, the new connection is created in the **old** diagram plane, not in the target Participant’s plane.  
   • That happens because **ReplaceConnectionBehavior** calls `modeling.connect(source, target, attrs)` with no parent hint, so the default LCA is wrong.  

2) Fix  
   Pass `{ parent: newParent }` as a hint to `modeling.connect`.  

